WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:09.577
The Ledger keeps the requirements, decisions and standing orders your agents rely on, so nobody has to ask the same question twice.

2
00:00:10.285 --> 00:00:15.380
Open Ledger in the sidebar. Search finds an entry by the words in it.

3
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:23.359
The chips show only standing orders, decisions or requirements, and the Project filter narrows the list to one project.

4
00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:36.888
Choose Add entry. A standing order is loaded by every agent. Leave the project blank and it applies to every project. Requirements and decisions always belong to one project.

5
00:00:37.588 --> 00:00:45.493
Give it a title and the text, then choose Add to ledger. Every agent loads the new order from its next shift or chat.

6
00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:58.132
A standing order can be edited. Agents get the new wording from their next shift, and the earlier wording stays in its history. History shows every version, who saved it, and when.

7
00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:07.077
An entry that no longer applies is retired, with a reason. Agents stop seeing it, and a search no longer finds it.

8
00:01:07.781 --> 00:01:13.017
Show retired brings retired entries back into view, greyed out, for the record.

9
00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:18.211
That is the Ledger: what your agents know, in one place you can search and correct.
